# Fixture for time_symbol_test (issue #87).  BNG2 rejects a parameter named
# `time` but accepts an observable named `time`; the call form `time()` is
# still the clock.  BNG2 also leaves `t` free, and a parameter named `t` is
# that parameter, not the clock.  A() never changes, so the observable `time`
# holds 5 for the whole run:
#
#   f() = k*(time+1)    reads the observable: 600, so B(t) has mean 600 t
#   g() = k*(time()+1)  reads the clock: 100 (t+1), so C(t) has mean 100 (t + t^2/2)
#   h() = 10*t          reads the parameter: 30 at every sample
begin model
begin parameters
  k 100
  t 3
end parameters
begin molecule types
  A()
  B()
  C()
end molecule types
begin seed species
  A() 5
  B() 0
  C() 0
end seed species
begin observables
  Molecules time A()
  Molecules Bobs B()
  Molecules Cobs C()
end observables
begin functions
  f() = k*(time+1)
  g() = k*(time()+1)
  h() = 10*t
end functions
begin reaction rules
  0 -> B() f()
  0 -> C() g()
end reaction rules
end model
begin actions
  writeXML()
end actions
